From 378ffab917d2c697378a21aa1c65b11a1b157c8a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 15:12:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(billing): real Stripe checkout, webhook fulfillment, and
 persisted billing
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Replaces the fake card-entry checkout form and always-succeeding mock payment
gateway with a real Stripe Checkout (subscription mode) redirect, plus a
webhook endpoint that verifies Stripe's signature and persists real
Subscription/Invoice/InvoiceItem/Payment records via Prisma against the
logged-in parent's real ParentProfile.id:

- src/lib/integrations/stripe.ts: lazy Stripe SDK client singleton (never
  crashes a page/build when STRIPE_SECRET_KEY isn't set; only errors when a
  checkout/webhook path actually needs it)
- src/server/services/StripeSubscriptionService.ts: creates the Checkout
  Session (reuses BillingService's existing plan/coupon pricing logic),
  fulfills checkout.session.completed, records invoice.paid renewals, and
  syncs subscription status on customer.subscription.updated/deleted. Maps
  the existing in-memory plan catalog to real Prisma Plan rows on demand
  (upsert-by-shape, since Plan has no natural unique key besides id).
- src/app/api/webhooks/stripe/route.ts: verifies the Stripe webhook
  signature against the raw request body and dispatches to the service above
- parent/checkout: removes the fake card fields entirely; "Confirm Payment"
  now redirects to Stripe's own hosted, PCI-compliant payment page
- parent/checkout/success: post-payment confirmation page
- parent/billing: now reads real Prisma subscription/invoice data instead of
  the always-empty-for-real-users in-memory mock
- parent/invoices/[id]: now scoped to the logged-in parent (previously
  looked up by URL id alone, with no ownership check) and reads real Prisma
  data

BillingService/FinancialRepository (the in-memory demo catalog) are left
untouched — they're still relied on by the admin dashboards, payroll, and
plan/coupon pricing math, none of which this change touches.

Verified against the actual installed stripe@22.6.2 SDK type definitions
(this sandbox has no network access to run `prisma generate`, so Prisma
enum-import errors from a stale generated client are expected locally and
are unrelated to this change — see tsc output).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
